\title{What a Verified zkVM Would Mean}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    The statement at the top of the whole effort, written out honestly: which theorems compose, and
    which links in the chain are assumptions rather than proofs. It is the claim the whole effort
    will be judged on, and its general form is [the issue of incorrect
    specification](dhsorens-001K): a machine-checked proof is only ever as good as the statement it
    proves.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{The chain: ISA specification, constraint system, arithmetisation soundness, IOP
        soundness, commitment security, [Fiat–Shamir](dhsorens-002G), recursion, extracted
        implementation.}
        \li{Which links are proved today, which are stated, and which are not formalised at all.}
        \li{The irreducible assumptions: [hash security](dhsorens-004D), [conjectured proximity
        bounds](dhsorens-0038), the compiler, the hardware.}
        \li{Whether "verified" should mean the composed end-to-end theorem, or a set of component
        theorems with audited seams.}
        \li{The 2027 target the project set, and what would have to be true for it to be met.}
    }
}

\p{
    Sources: [verified-zkevm.org](https://verified-zkevm.org), [Verified-zkEVM
    overview](https://github.com/Verified-zkEVM/Overview).
}
